WEBVTT

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:07.980
Hello, I'm Kurata Ami!

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.560
These days, I commute to
school and work on Ponta-kun,

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.400
and ride my road bike on the weekend!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.740
I spend a whole lot more time with bicycles now!

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.280
Since I recently set a goal to
participate in the Azumino Autumn Ride,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.760
I'm starting to love cycling more and more!

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.850
G-Good morning, Saeki-san.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.390
G-Good morning...

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.120
Kurata-san.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.460
Umm...!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.050
Um, please, Saeki-san, you first.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.670
Kurata-san, you bike to school?

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:48.640
Yeah, at the start of school, I took the bus,

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.260
but now, I'm hooked on my bike.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.690
Hooked on your bike?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.030
Yes!

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.320
I began cycling.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.030
I trip all the time even when I'm walking normally,

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.900
and I'm not very physical.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:06.890
At first, I thought cycling would be impossible for me.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.950
But once I got started,
it was actually really fun!

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:14.880
I even bought a road bike!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.220
And I'm entering my very first
cycling event with everyone!

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.720
With everyone? An event?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.020
I have some friends who cycle together with me.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.470
And we formed a team so we can all ride together!

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:31.980
That sounds really nice.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:39.480
Oh, but... I'm a little worried
that I might hold them back.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.490
Saeki-san?

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:47.610
Yeah.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.620
Oh... that quiet girl.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.000
I hadn't spoken to her much either,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.250
but she asked me about my bike in class.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.100
Is she interested in cycling?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.380
I didn't get to ask her specifically...

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.710
But we had a lively conversation about the cycling event.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:08.920
Although...

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.560
I did most of the talking.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.460
I'm seeing a glimmer of hope

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.640
A glimmer?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.140
Hinako-chan's purpose in life
is to make more cycling friends.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.870
Don't say that as if I'm some lonely old person

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:27.160
Anyway, Hinako-chan has a suggestion for our next cycling tour.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.350
In preparation for the Azumino Autumn Ride...

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.670
I came up with a 100-kilo course that Ami can try.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.080
So she can physically experience long-distance rides beforehand?

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.710
That's right.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.550
But... 100 kilos sounds so unbelievable.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.810
What're you saying?
The Autumn Ride is 160 kilometers.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.060
160 kilometers?!

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:58.310
I don't think I'm capable of that without a miracle...

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.260
Of all the courses Ami's experienced...

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.780
Otarumi Pass was the longest, at about 70 kilometers.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:08.380
So a 100-km event means 30 kilometers longer.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.480
30 kilometers?

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:12.830
Will I be able to complete the course?

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:14.500
Don't worry!

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.350
We'll start from Kasai
and go through the Arakawa cycling path

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.460
to Ogawamachi in Saitama. It's a pretty flat ride.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.840
And we can rest as we go.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.400
I think you're absolutely
capable of it now, Ami-chan.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.980
And there are so many great places to eat along the way.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:37.940
It's a course hand-picked to let
Ami-chan enjoy it to the fullest, right?

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.420
Well, yeah...

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.940
Riding farther is easier when it's fun.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.530
Guys...

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.680
I want to experience cycling 100 kilometers!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.960
Then it's decided.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:03.290
I can't wait!

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.480
I, Kurata Ami, will do my best!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.540
Onee-chan!

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.180
It's time for dinner.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.600
Emi?!

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.980
Ami, you've been eating a lot lately.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.620
Huh? Really?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.060
Won't you get fat if you eat that much?

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:35.490
It's okay! I'm burning it all off on my bike!

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.210
I see...

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.250
Probably...

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.640
Okay then, shall we get going?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.890
Yes!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.900
Ami-chan, you seem really motivated.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.020
It's my first 100 kilo ride, after all.

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:08.780
Well, it's a flat course.
Let's take it easy and enjoy ourselves

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.280
Yeah!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.860
Are you ready?

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:12.720
Yes!

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.760
Okay, let's go!

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:24.310
We're getting a slight headwind, but it's not bad, is it?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.810
Not at all, it feels good!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.570
Something delicious is waiting for us at the next rest stop.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.570
"Something delicious"?
What is it? What is it?

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.580
That's a surprise.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.580
I can't wait!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.590
Delicious!

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:55.590
This store is right along our route at the point where we need our first break, so we always stop here.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.470
The vanilla is the best!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.940
What about you, Aoi-chan?
What flavor did you get?

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.020
Strawberry. Yours?

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.650
It's caramel.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:05.280
Here.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.610
Mmm, it's good!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.130
Right?

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.650
Here.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.830
This is good too.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.530
Ami... It seems like you still have lots of energy.

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.250
Yes, I'm pumped up!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.910
That's the way to go!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.410
We can visit a bunch of places
when we ride our bikes, can't we?

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:34.350
Yeah!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:40.140
Well, that's one of the pleasures of cycling.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.480
Cycling...

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:49.040
Your world keeps expanding, doesn't it, Ami?

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.760
Enjoying it?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:01.520
Isn't it good?

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.660
Yes! It's great, isn't it?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:06.320
Yeah. So next is...

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.440
This pastry has totally re-energized me!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:17.930
I feel like I can achieve 100 kilometers!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.900
There's a place called Matsugo Pass up ahead.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:26.560
That's the only spot that's actually a little uphill. So hang in there.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:30.310
Yes! I definitely want to complete the course!

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:45.040
You okay, Ami?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:45.930
Yeah!

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.740
You did it, Ami!

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.850
You finally conquered 100 kilometers!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:08.850
As long as you're not too caught up about the distance, it's possible to go quite far.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.860
Congratulations, Ami!

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.230
Yeah!

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:21.200
All right, let's make it all the way to Ogawamachi Station!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.360
Yes!

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.630
Good job!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.440
Thank you!

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:40.090
How do you feel after cycling over 100 kilometers?

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.880
It feels amazing!

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:44.890
You have that written all over your face.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:51.540
At first, I really couldn't imagine myself riding a bike...

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.900
for 100 kilometers!

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:56.470
But... you accomplished it!

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.030
Ami, I think you still have some energy to spare.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.310
Huh? Think so?

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:06.910
At this rate, you'll do fine in the 160 kilo Autumn Ride!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.160
Yes!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.410
Let's do our best.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:10.660
Yes!

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.170
Let's see...

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.300
Do you have extra clothes?

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:22.220
You should pack bandages and stuff.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.650
You tend to fall a lot.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.800
That's true.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:29.330
I wish you'd take the entire first-aid box.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:32.810
Don't overeat and get a tummy-ache.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.620
I'm not in grade school, you know.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.310
But I can't help but worry...

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.440
You'll be spending two nights away with just the girls.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:45.720
Well, Aoi-chan is going too,
so I guess there's no reason to worry.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:49.350
But Onee-chan, are you really going to be okay?

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:52.320
You'll be riding a bike for 160 kilometers!

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:55.820
I'm not sure if I can complete it.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:57.330
But...

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:00.460
Aoi-chan and the others will be with me!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.320
I want to test myself!

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:05.480
Onee-chan...

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.220
Go for it, then!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.350
Have lots of fun.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:13.980
Uh-huh!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.320
Yayoi-san, you're really good at driving.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:45.630
But my breasts get in the way
when I turn the steering wheel.

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.010
Oh, should I take your place, then?

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.290
I don't have that handicap.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:54.240
Oh, Hinako-san, you can drive too?

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:58.160
Mmm, she can, but when I have Hinako-chan drive...

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:01.200
there's an entirely different cause for concern...

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.270
Concern?

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.510
Didn't you see the scratch on the body?

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.780
I-I just had a little bad luck that one time.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.880
But you can't see your surroundings too well
from the driver's seat, can you?

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:15.290
That's where my exceptional instincts come in.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:20.100
I'm sorry, Yayoi-san...
please continue driving.

00:14:20.100 --> 00:14:21.870
I think that's a good idea.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.190
Why?

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:37.060
All those people are going to participate in the Autumn Ride too?

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.580
Matsumoto Station will be jammed with cyclists packing bikes.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:44.490
I wonder if Saki-san is already there?

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.720
Of course!

00:14:45.720 --> 00:14:47.320
Should I try calling her?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:51.160
Nah, she probably got there early
and is walking around eating.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:55.830
Probably. She actually replied to our message today.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.800
When we get to the site, we register,
have a security check for our belongings,

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.870
and then get our race numbers, right?

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:02.840
Yeah.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.120
Register...

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.550
Security check...

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.860
Get our race numbers!

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:10.560
Now then, we're almost there.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:18.880
The pre-event bike training seminar is going to start.

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:22.860
If you are interested, please gather around the main stage!

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.090
Wow!

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:30.360
Every year, the number of applicants rises.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:35.440
The Azumino Autumn Ride is popular because the food is so good.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:40.060
It's limited to the first 1500 who sign up and fills up quickly,

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:42.880
so I'm sure there are many who can't participate.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:45.770
It really is a popular event...

00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.880
Now then, let's register too.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.080
Yes!

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.380
First, we register...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:56.890
and the security check, then...

00:15:58.670 --> 00:16:00.340
Oh, um...!

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:02.020
Thank you!

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:05.400
Good luck.

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:16.270
Did everyone get their race numbers?

00:16:16.270 --> 00:16:18.630
Okay, let's go to the inn.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:19.790
Yes!

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.910
Tonight's inn was recommended by Yayoi!

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.420
Please look forward to it.

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:27.420
Yes!

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:35.880
Oh, the atmosphere of this inn is great!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:38.160
It's really tasteful.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.680
Here we are!

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.640
I chose a Japanese-style room.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:47.690
Five of us sharing this room was cheaper than two western-style rooms.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.740
I've got to hand it to you, Yayoi-san!

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:54.470
Five of us together will be fun!
It's just like a school trip!

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.150
I wish Saki-san would hurry.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:00.320
Don't worry. Our reservation includes dinner.

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:02.890
She'll show up by that time.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:05.530
I think so, too.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.550
It's so spacious!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:17.840
There's a private bath, but we prefer the main communal bath, right?

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:20.470
How about a soak before dinner?

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.200
Yes!

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:21.960
Let's!

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.720
Doesn't this feel great?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:33.750
Yeah.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:36.010
This is paradise.

00:17:36.010 --> 00:17:39.240
Ami-chan, I knew you'd say that.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.080
Hinako-chan, you always say the same thing.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:45.270
Well, paradise is the only way to describe this.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.640
But... the disparity between those who are blessed and those who aren't...

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.480
that does bother me a bit.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:59.280
Ami, you're on my side.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.780
Ah, I'm starving!

00:18:05.780 --> 00:18:07.640
Yes, I'm hungry.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:12.140
The dinner here includes all kinds of local delicacies.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.540
I can't wait!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.870
Saki-san should be here soon, right?

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.400
She should.

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:19.660
Don't worry about her.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.660
Saki-chan's never late for a meal.

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:33.670
Come on, everyone! It's delicious.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.070
See?

00:18:35.070 --> 00:18:36.450
You're right.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:38.480
You're already having seconds?

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.310
That's our Saki-san.

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:43.930
Hey, you could've at least waited for us.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:47.210
It's okay! I just started eating.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.830
Just how much do you plan to eat?!

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:51.100
A decent portion of the rice is already gone.

00:19:05.420 --> 00:19:08.000
I'm getting a little nervous.

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.010
What is it, Ami?

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.330
I'm starting to get nervous.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.860
Here, have some herbal tea.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:32.350
It's your first time. I figured you'd be nervous.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.510
I brought an herbal tea that has relaxant properties.

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:37.860
Thank you, Aoi-chan!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:44.860
It warms me up.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:46.230
I'm glad.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.030
Thank you.

00:19:49.030 --> 00:19:51.120
I feel much calmer.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.520
Let's go at our pace tomorrow. No need to stress.

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:56.970
Yes!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.630
Are you up?

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:14.900
You look well rested.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.300
Yes...

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:18.790
Good morning!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.700
Hurry and change.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.260
It's the big day.

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:24.530
Let's do our best.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.640
Yes!

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.840
They all seem fast.

00:20:39.840 --> 00:20:43.070
It's not a race. Take it easy and just have fun.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.050
Everyone gathered here to have fun.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.200
See?

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.320
Over there too.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.810
You're right.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.620
You have to have fun at these events.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:57.190
You're right.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.560
It's a 160-kilo event,

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:04.440
but they allot plenty of time to finish. So don't worry.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:05.700
O-Okay...

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.580
The Azumino Autumn Ride!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.990
Group One, start!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.600
The lead group is starting.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:25.780
We'll be starting soon too.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.550
I'm so excited.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.060
Our goal is just to complete the course.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:31.470
Let's have fun.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.300
Yeah!

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:35.480
Our goal is...

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.480
to have fun...

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.920
and to complete the course...

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.230
all together!

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:33.850
